#: weui_zlibrary_proxy.lua
msgid ""
"Only Z-Library traffic uses this proxy, including login, search, covers, book downloads, mirror discovery, favorites, and Z-Library updates.\n"
"\n"
"HTTP proxies use CONNECT for HTTPS. SOCKS5 sends target hostnames to the proxy for remote DNS resolution. A proxy failure always blocks the request; there is no direct fallback. Use only a proxy server you trust.\n"
"\n"
"127.0.0.1 means the Kindle itself. For a proxy running on a computer, phone, or router, enter its LAN IP and allow LAN connections. Using a proxy IP also avoids a local DNS lookup for the proxy server."
